// REQUIRES: long, host-linux-amd64, qemu-aarch64
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/run-opt-matrix.py --gopp %gopp --root %S --target arm64 --sysroot %aarch64_sysroot --jobs 8 --verify-dwarf --shard 0/3
// RUN: %if clang %{ %python %S/Inputs/run-opt-matrix.py --gopp %gopp --root %S --target arm64 --sysroot %aarch64_sysroot --jobs 8 --verify-dwarf --no-corpus --cabi 3:25 --cabi 4:25 %}
// P04.12: and `llvm-dwarfdump --verify` accepts the DWARF of every program.
// P04.13 (D4.8): the whole run corpus at every `opt` level and with
// -pipeline=fastisel on linux/arm64 under QEMU, and with clang the C ABI
// programs of seeds 3 and 4 (cabi-arm64.test). See core-opt-matrix.test and
// core-opt-matrix.long.test.
// The corpus runs in 3 shards side by side (core-opt-matrix-arm64.long.test and
// core-opt-matrix-arm64-2.long.test to -3.long.test: the programs whose place in the
// sorted corpus is K modulo 3, every configuration of each;
// core-opt-matrix-shards.test checks that together they are the whole
// corpus, each program once); the C ABI programs are in the first.
